# Unblessed: Session Store Notifications, the specification's example (#621); first blessing awaits human review.
# A commit that changes a watched key delivers the Handler, in a background
# Run, at the same Clock reading. A write that changes nothing sends nothing.
# :store clear is routed; :restore brings the watch back, resynced because the
# Store changed after :save, so its marker's keys is [].
> :grant scores store
> :clock virtual 2026-09-30T10:00:00Z
> on scoresChanged change, queued
|   say the "keys" of change
| end scoresChanged
> ask scores to watch "all", "", "scoresChanged"
> ask scores to set "alex", 3
[session/r3] ["alex"]
> ask scores to set "alex", 3
> :save
saved default
> :store clear
cleared default
[session/r5] ["alex"]
> :restore
restored default
[session/r5] []
